#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md:6
msgid "Declarative Macro Techniques"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md:8
msgid ""
"As your declarative macros become more sophisticated, simple patterns may "
"not be enough to express your intended logic."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md:11
msgid ""
"Rust programmers have established several design patterns for structuring "
"more complex macros:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md:14
msgid ""
"**Optional Parameters:** Using multiple match arms or optional matchers to "
"handle default values."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md:16
msgid ""
"**Named Parameters:** Explicitly labeling parameters at the callsite (e.g., "
"`key=value`) to improve readability."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md:18
msgid ""
"**Internal Rules:** Prefixing helper match arms with a unique symbol (like "
"`@`) to modularize code."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md:20
msgid ""
"**Incremental Token Munchers:** Eating tokens off the front of a stream "
"recursively."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md:22
msgid ""
"**Push-Down Accumulators:** Collecting tokens recursively into a buffer to "
"build a structured output."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md:24
msgid ""
"**TT Bundling:** Grouping multiple arguments inside a single Token Tree to "
"simplify passing them down."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md:27
msgid "We will consider each of these advanced techniques in turn."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md:32
msgid ""
"Reassure students that these patterns are standard idioms in advanced Rust "
"code bases, but not necessary for simple macros. A programmer must use their "
"discretion to choose between a complex declarative macro and implementing "
"logic in a procedural macro, which may be more straightforward at the cost "
"of additional ceremony."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/techniques.md:37
msgid ""
"Explain that because declarative macros don't have standard local variables "
"or mutable state during expansion, recursion and token-level manipulation "
"are the primary ways to achieve complex code generation."
msgstr ""
